      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Los dioses llevaron a Fenrir a una isla llamada Lyngvi, y le mostraron la cinta delgada.",
          "en": "The gods led Fenrir to an island called Lyngvi, and showed him the slender ribbon."
        },
        {
          "es": "El lobo desconfió. Era muy fina para ser tan fuerte, y dijo que no se dejaría atar si había un engaño.",
          "en": "The wolf was wary. It was too thin to be so strong, and he said he would not be bound if there was any trickery."
        },
        {
          "es": "Pero para no parecer cobarde, pidió que uno de los dioses pusiera la mano en su boca, como garantía.",
          "en": "But so as not to seem a coward, he asked that one of the gods lay a hand in his mouth as a pledge."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los dioses se miraron, y ninguno se movió. Entonces Tyr puso su mano derecha entre los dientes del lobo.",
          "en": "The gods looked at one another, and no one moved. Then Tyr put his right hand between the wolf's teeth."
        },
        {
          "es": "Fenrir luchó, pero cuanto más tiraba, más se apretaba la cinta. Todos los dioses rieron, menos Tyr.",
          "en": "Fenrir fought, but the harder he pulled, the tighter the ribbon grew. All the gods laughed, except Tyr."
        },
        {
          "es": "Y por eso Tyr es el dios manco: pagó con su mano la palabra que los dioses le habían dado al lobo.",
          "en": "And that is why Tyr is the one-handed god: he paid with his hand for the word the gods had given the wolf."
        }
      ],
